Subject: [PATCH] W-32: EDEN_MIC_FEED and EDEN_MIC_DUMP index lines for the whole session, not the first 200

The feed and dump index lines shared a cap of 200 lines, so they stopped about a minute after the
game opened its raw mic stream (W-24 at 779 s, W-30 at 104 s) and never covered the hums. Now each
has its own pacer (common/nx2_mic_log.h): the first 200 lines of the session as before, then a line
whenever the indices moved since the last line, and every 10 s otherwise. Still only with
EDEN_UP_MIC_DUMP / EDEN_UP_MIC_FEED set. Host test: tools/test-mic-log.cpp (outer repo).

